{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3780","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3780","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3780\",\"parent_revision\":\"d30f4a7ff4e5882a7f08357ccf983a566ba2b001\",\"root_revision\":\"56a9da4cb65fd42e430f980a9045bcaf61d93f51919b3f1d7d043fc06f76b1bb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: completed\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe repository fast test suite passes but emits 144 warnings. Observed categories include MCP logging deprecations, Typer option deprecations, and PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning from dh_paths hanging-stub threads leaking into later dispatch-schema tests. Warning output obscures regressions and contradicts the repository validation policy that warnings should be resolved or explicitly scoped.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:48:59.457994Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: The full fast suite passes while emitting 144 warnings in three categories.\\nevidence: Bounded `uv run pytest` completed with `6591 passed, 54 skipped, 10 xfailed, 144 warnings`; summary grouped 44 MCPDeprecationWarning, 96 Typer DeprecationWarning, and 4 PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning emissions.\\nsource: local bounded reproduction on 2026-09-21.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: FastMCP client logging emits a deprecation under the installed 4.0.2 behavior.\\nevidence: Warning-as-error reproduction failed at `server.py:2609` -> `ctx.info` -> `fastmcp/server/context.py:1357` with `MCPDeprecationWarning: The logging capability is deprecated as of 2026-07-28 (SEP-2577)`. FastMCP 4.0.0 documents support for the 2026-07-28 protocol and deprecation/removal of server push-era capabilities.\\nsource: https://gofastmcp.com/changelog.md and installed FastMCP 4.0.2 runtime traceback.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Typer 0.27.0 warns whenever `is_flag` or `flag_value` is non-None.\\nevidence: Upstream `OptionInfo.__init__` explicitly calls `warnings.warn` when either value is non-None; local source passes `is_flag=True` four times, and warning-as-error produces seven deterministic test failures in one affected file.\\nsource: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fastapi/typer/0.27.0/typer/models.py and https://typer.tiangolo.com/reference/parameters/.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Hanging-stub daemon threads escape their owning tests and raise in later tests.\\nevidence: The red-capable sequence failed later in `TestDispatchSpawn::test_spawn_end_to_end_single_wave` with an ExceptionGroup containing four `PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning` instances; every traceback ends at `test_dh_paths.py:337` after `dh_paths.py:122`.\\nsource: local warning-as-error reproduction on 2026-09-21.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:47:09.598875Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: Eliminate full test suite warning output\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\nGoal: Remove every observed warning from the fast test suite by correcting each emitting code or test lifecycle.\\nConditions:\\n1. Warning categories and counts are reproducible | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Current FastMCP logging behavior is verified from primary upstream/runtime sources | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Current Typer option behavior is verified from primary upstream sources | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Thread-warning trigger and ownership are identified | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Affected systems and deterministic validation commands are known | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T04:14:11.098731Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: fix: Eliminate full test suite warning output\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\nGoal: Remove every observed warning from the fast test suite by correcting each emitting code or test lifecycle without warning suppression or dependency downgrade.\\n\\nRT-ICA SUMMARY\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Eliminate the 144 observed fast-suite warnings while preserving backlog operation payloads, migration CLI semantics, and production git-resolution timeout behavior.\\n\\nSuccess Output:\\n- The bounded fast suite and all three category-specific warning-as-error reproductions exit zero with no warnings summary.\\n\\nScope Boundaries:\\n- In scope: deprecated FastMCP context logging calls, deprecated explicit Typer boolean option metadata, synthetic timeout-worker ownership and cleanup, directly affected tests, and focused/full validation.\\n- Out of scope: warning filters, dependency downgrades, broad production exception suppression, dispatch-test changes, and unrelated refactoring.\\n\\nConditions (reverse prerequisites):\\n1. Warning baseline is reproducible | Requires: category counts and deterministic commands | Why: establishes observable red/green loops.\\n2. FastMCP emitting calls and preserved behavior are known | Requires: deprecated call sites, affected tests, response/error contract | Why: transport progress removal must not alter business-operation output.\\n3. Typer emitting options and preserved flags are known | Requires: all explicit is_flag call sites and CLI behavior tests | Why: deprecation removal must retain boolean semantics.\\n4. Thread-warning owner and lifecycle correction are known | Requires: delayed stub traceback, owning tests, production visibility constraint | Why: cleanup must fix test isolation without hiding production defects.\\n5. Impact set and validation gates are known | Requires: canonical Systems Inventory, acceptance criteria, focused lint/type/test and bounded suite commands | Why: planning must cover every affected system and prove zero warnings.\\n6. Prohibited alternatives are explicit | Requires: no warning suppression, dependency downgrade, broad production catch, or dispatch-test workaround | Why: prevents symptom masking and deferred breakage.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- Warning baseline: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Fact-Check and Reproducibility record 6591 passed, 54 skipped, 10 xfailed, 144 warnings and all deterministic red commands.\\n- FastMCP path: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Root-Cause Analysis plus 15 resolving ctx.info/ctx.warning call sites in backlog_core/server.py and affected consumer tests in Impact Radius.\\n- Typer path: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Root-Cause Analysis plus four resolving is_flag=True call sites across both migration CLIs and their tests.\\n- Thread lifecycle: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Root-Cause Analysis, deterministic thread red reproduction, and test_dh_paths.py synthetic _hang ownership; production dh_paths.py remains verification-only unless evidence changes.\\n- Impact and validation: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: eight canonical Systems Inventory rows, seven Acceptance Criteria, and focused/full commands in Reproducibility.\\n- Guardrails: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Design Intent Alignment and Root-Cause Analysis explicitly rule out suppression, downgrade, broad catches, and dispatch-test changes.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n\\nAssumptions to Confirm (EVIDENCE-DERIVED only):\\n- Removing transport-side progress logging is behavior-preserving because operation result payloads and errors are independently asserted | Basis: Design Intent Alignment and Acceptance Criterion 3 | Validation step: run affected backlog MCP operation tests plus FastMCP warning-as-error reproduction.\\n\\nSafe Defaults Applied (SAFE-DEFAULTED only):\\n- None.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:49:50.583400Z</sub>\\n\\nType: recurring-pattern\\nRationale: Three independent obsolete or unmanaged lifecycle patterns produce the same validation failure class, and each repeats across multiple calls/tests.\\nAnalysis Method: 6-sigma category measurement plus evidence-chain root-cause analysis.\\nScenario Target: fast suite passes with 144 warnings -> fast suite passes with zero warnings and category-specific warning-as-error checks pass.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:57:22.698233Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`\\n- Other MCP tests listed in Impact Radius, only where expectations require adjustment\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/verify_migration_fidelity.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_verify_migration_fidelity.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dh_paths.py`\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` is verification-only unless implementation proves production ownership is necessary; the current evidence places the leak in the synthetic test stub.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:58:12.086377Z</sub>\\n\\n- FastMCP current changelog and protocol migration: https://gofastmcp.com/changelog.md\\n- FastMCP current logging documentation: https://gofastmcp.com/servers/logging\\n- Typer 0.27.0 option implementation: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fastapi/typer/0.27.0/typer/params.py\\n- Typer 0.27.0 warning implementation: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fastapi/typer/0.27.0/typer/models.py\\n- Typer current parameter reference: https://typer.tiangolo.com/reference/parameters/\\n- Repository test policy: `docs/testing.md`\\n- Backlog package boundary: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:54:01.278772Z</sub>\\n\\n- Validation logs contain 144 non-actionable warnings despite a passing suite.\\n- Deprecated FastMCP and Typer calls are on removal paths and can become hard failures on upgrades.\\n- Escaped test threads violate test isolation and assign failures to unrelated later tests.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:48:06.198918Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: 13 files across MCP runtime/tests, migration CLIs/tests, and path-resolution tests.\\n\\n### Code - Producers (write the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` - 15 `ctx.info`/`ctx.warning` calls invoke deprecated MCP client logging.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` - three boolean options explicitly pass unsupported `is_flag=True`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/verify_migration_fidelity.py` - one boolean option explicitly passes unsupported `is_flag=True`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` - timeout worker intentionally leaves unexpected exceptions to thread reporting; production behavior is valid, but tests must not leave their synthetic workers to raise after teardown.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` - asserts deprecated context logging and tool behavior.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_groom_sections.py` - exercises groom paths that emit context logging.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_frontend_parity_ops.py` - exercises logging-emitting MCP operations.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` - exercises logging-emitting sync scenarios.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_validator_escape_classification.py` - exercises logging-emitting pull/sync paths.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` - invokes the affected Typer CLI.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_verify_migration_fidelity.py` - invokes the affected Typer CLI.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dh_paths.py` - owns the delayed `_hang` stub and its cleanup lifecycle.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` - deterministic downstream collection point used by the thread-warning reproduction; no source change expected.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\nNone identified; user-visible CLI behavior is unchanged.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n- `pyproject.toml` - strict warning behavior and dependency versions are validation context; no suppression or downgrade change permitted.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n1. Backlog MCP tool progress reporting -> FastMCP Context -> deprecated MCP logging capability.\\n2. MCP server tests -> in-memory FastMCP client -> warning collection.\\n3. Backlog migration CLI -> Typer option metadata -> CLI parser construction.\\n4. Migration fidelity CLI -> Typer option metadata -> CLI parser construction.\\n5. Migration CLI tests -> Typer runner -> repeated warning emission.\\n6. Git project-root timeout -> daemon worker thread -> queue handoff.\\n7. Hanging-path tests -> delayed synthetic exception -> pytest threadexception hook.\\n8. Dispatch tests -> later test activity long enough to collect escaped thread exceptions.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every listed producer corrected or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected consumer test updated\\n- [ ] No warning filters or dependency downgrades added\\n- [ ] CLI semantics retained\\n- [ ] Full bounded fast suite reports zero warnings\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:53:11.389696Z</sub>\\n\\nPriority: P2\\nEffort: MEDIUM\\nRationale: The suite passes, so delivery is not blocked, but warning volume masks future regressions and all warnings violate the repository validation policy. Scope spans three independent corrections and their focused tests.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:54:51.528108Z</sub>\\n\\n- Restores warning-free validation signal without suppression.\\n- Keeps migration CLIs compatible with current Typer while preserving flags.\\n- Makes timeout tests deterministic and prevents cross-test contamination.\\n- Converts each warning category into an executable regression gate.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:51:33.212202Z</sub>\\n\\nMISSION_ALIGNED\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\nThe change supports the repository validation policy in `docs/testing.md`: warnings fail validation unless a versioned, scope-limited exception is recorded. Removing deprecated API usage and ensuring test-owned cleanup also follows `ARCHITECTURE.md` acceptance-criterion guidance that verification must be machine-runnable, and `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` keeps MCP wrappers thin around operations. No architecture boundary change is required.\\n\\nConstraint: preserve business-operation output and provider boundaries; replace only deprecated transport-side progress behavior. Preserve `dh_paths.py` production policy of exposing unexpected worker exceptions; repair synthetic test lifecycle instead.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:56:32.727025Z</sub>\\n\\n1. The bounded full fast suite exits zero and emits zero warnings.\\n2. The FastMCP warning-as-error reproduction exits zero without `MCPDeprecationWarning`; no warning filter or dependency downgrade is added.\\n3. All backlog MCP operation tests retain response messages/errors and no test asserts deprecated protocol logging.\\n4. Both migration CLIs preserve `--dry-run`, `--confirm`, `--cleanup`, and `--verbose` behavior while the Typer warning-as-error tests exit zero.\\n5. The thread warning-as-error sequence exits zero; every synthetic timeout worker is deterministically released and completed by its owning test.\\n6. Production git-resolution timeout behavior and unexpected-exception visibility remain covered.\\n7. Focused changed-file lint/type/test gates pass.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:55:45.472251Z</sub>\\n\\nThe bounded fast suite completes with its existing pass/skip/xfail behavior and no warnings summary. Focused warning-as-error commands for MCP logging, Typer option construction, and timeout-worker cleanup all exit zero. Backlog operation result payloads, migration CLI flags, and git-resolution timeout semantics remain unchanged.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:52:24.793454Z</sub>\\n\\nDeterministic on Python 3.13.15, pytest 9.1.1, FastMCP 4.0.2, Typer 0.27.0.\\n\\n- Full bounded suite: `uv run --script scripts/run_bounded.py --timeout-seconds 600 -- uv run pytest -m \\\"not e2e and not cross_backend and not integration and not research_vault and not slow\\\"` -> PASS with 144 warnings.\\n- FastMCP red check: `uv run pytest -n 0 --no-cov -W error::mcp.shared.exceptions.MCPDeprecationWarning plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py::test_backlog_sync_success_returns_counts` -> FAIL at `ctx.info`.\\n- Typer red check: `uv run pytest -n 0 --no-cov -W error::DeprecationWarning plugins/development-harness/tests/test_migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` -> 7 failed, 6 passed.\\n- Thread red check: `uv run pytest -n 0 --no-cov -W error::pytest.PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dh_paths.py::TestGitCommonRootHangProtection plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_state.py plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` -> 1 failed, 73 passed with four delayed `_hang` exceptions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed while validating #3778\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:50:42.000019Z</sub>\\n\\n**Measured categories**: FastMCP logging 44, Typer options 96, escaped thread exceptions 4.\\n\\n**Root cause**: Validation dependencies advanced across explicit deprecation/lifecycle boundaries while repository call sites and test doubles retained obsolete assumptions.\\n\\n1. FastMCP: backlog MCP wrappers use Context client-log methods for progress; FastMCP 4.0.2 routes those calls through the protocol logging capability, which warns under the 2026-07-28 protocol.\\n2. Typer: two migration CLIs explicitly set `is_flag=True`; Typer 0.27.0 infers boolean flags and warns on either explicit `is_flag` or `flag_value`.\\n3. Threads: timeout tests create daemon workers whose synthetic `_hang` sleeps beyond the assertion and then raises after monkeypatch teardown; pytest collects those unowned exceptions during later tests.\\n\\n**Systemic correction**: remove obsolete API arguments/calls and make every synthetic worker test-owned through deterministic release and cleanup. Preserve operation result messages, boolean CLI semantics, timeout behavior, and unexpected production exception reporting.\\n\\n**Ruled out**:\\n- Warning filters or pytest configuration changes: hide the failure and violate repository policy.\\n- Dependency downgrade/pin: retains obsolete behavior and defers breakage.\\n- Catching all production thread exceptions: masks genuine GitPython/wrapper defects that `dh_paths.py` intentionally exposes.\\n- Changing dispatch tests: they only reveal a worker escaped from `test_dh_paths.py`; they do not own the defect.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Migration Fidelity Exception\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T05:11:38.727015Z</sub>\\n\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\nAuthorized by: user during work #3780\\nDecision: NOT APPLICABLE\\nReason: The lexical detector matched migration utility filenames and prose about those CLIs. This change removes deprecated Typer option metadata and does not migrate, convert, replace, delete, or transition persisted source data. No source records or target model are involved, so real-data migration fidelity criteria have no applicable subject. Authorization is scoped only to #3780; all remaining complete-implementation gates still apply.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Feasibility Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T04:15:13.351343Z</sub>\\n\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\nResult: PASS\\n\\n**Technical path**: VERIFIED \u2014 all 13 Impact Radius files resolve; `backlog_core/server.py` contains 15 deprecated `ctx.info`/`ctx.warning` calls, the migration CLIs contain four explicit `is_flag=True` arguments, and `tests/test_dh_paths.py` contains the synthetic `_hang` owner. The absent Suggested Location is replaced by the issue Files and canonical Impact Radius inventories.\\n**Effort tier**: MEDIUM \u2014 proportionate to P2 because the work is three bounded corrections plus focused and full-suite verification.\\n**Blast radius**: 8 systems in the estimated impact set\\n**Prior attempts**: Reproducibility contains `7 failed` from the intentional Typer warning-as-error red check; no prior implementation attempt is recorded. Carry the deterministic red result into planning.\\n**Warnings**: Prior-attempt literal check matched the recorded red-test failure; include the reproduction in the feature request.\\n**Pattern refresh**: Not applicable \u2014 no complete pattern annotations\\n\\nCriterion 1 \u2014 Technical feasibility: PASS. Observable check: all canonical affected paths exist and referenced APIs resolve through fixed code search.\\nCriterion 2 \u2014 Effort proportionality: PASS. Observable check: Priority=P2 and Effort=MEDIUM.\\nCriterion 3 \u2014 Blast radius: PASS. Observable check: 8 distinct Systems Inventory rows; no pattern/pattern_count annotations; below the 11-system warning threshold.\\nCriterion 4 \u2014 Prior attempt/over-engineering: PASS WITH WARN. Observable check: literal `failed` appears only in deterministic red reproduction; canonical Systems Inventory has no file-valued rows and Effort has 0 checkbox task entries, so the one-file/four-task block is false.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e6fac3c1712fb76a03f83318faa795c65f1b3c17e9b2e1983640034857e91901\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABWMk8rg\"}"}